   141	## Gate results
   142	
   143	### Gate A — PASS
   144	
   145	- **A1 program identity/body sensitivity:** both entry claims load the exact
   146	  `FuncDef` body represented by `STRONGEST-BODY`, resolve its module binding,
   147	  and call that closure. `solution.mpy` was regenerated from `solution.py`.
   148	  Replacing the body by `Return(Str("wrong"))` makes the original result claim
   149	  fail.
   150	- **A2 operational-state preservation:** every bridge has an exact state
   151	  footprint and a connection theorem. Inner and outer bridges constrain all
   152	  changed locals in a closed plain frame; other top cells are framed equally
   153	  in bridge and theorem.
   154	- **A3 binding/evaluation/control fidelity:** the yield twin matches the exact
   155	  target and body; loop bridges match exact loop terms and preserve arbitrary
   156	  continuations. Each supporting theorem has the same continuation
   157	  generality. Projection identity and wrong-value rejection establish value
   158	  fidelity.
   159	- **A4 consistency/rule validity:** score cases are disjoint, scan branches are
   160	  true/false complements, recursive summaries descend, and total functions
   161	  cover their stated sorts. `codesProject` is opaque outside the guarded string
   162	  domain and no target use observes that region.
   163	- **A5 result constraint/non-vacuity:** the realizable empty/empty input returns
   164	  `"."`; mutating the result to `"X"` produces a stuck claim and exit `1`.
   165	
   166	### Gate B — PASS
   167	
   168	The formal domain is not length-bounded: it covers every finite class-name
   169	string and every finite list of finite extension strings in the fixed model.
   170	Empty lists are handled rather than excluded. Non-string extension elements
   171	are outside the prompt's extension-name domain and would make the specified
   172	character-method computation undefined.
   173	
   174	There is one explicit fixed-model boundary. CPython string case predicates are
   175	Unicode-aware, while the supplied semantics' `isUpperC`/`isLowerC` recognize
   176	ASCII ranges only, and source string literal loading is ASCII-only. The proof
   177	covers every `IntSeq` value represented by the fixed model and the implementation
   178	faithfully calls Python's `str.isupper`/`str.islower`; no theorem-side length or
   179	constructor restriction is introduced. Therefore this is a recorded language
   180	model boundary under Gate B2, not candidate domain narrowing. For example,
   181	CPython treats Greek `Ω` as uppercase, while the fixed predicate does not.
   182	
   183	The scan summary-to-property bridge is formal: its strict-update recursive
   184	equations select the first maximum, and the unbounded outer connection theorem
   185	proves the program implements those equations.
   186	
